    {
      "id": "3jzaowu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Banking"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) acts as the central banking authority controlling credit, currency issuance, and monetary policy.",
        "Commercial banks are divided into scheduled and non-scheduled banks, covering public sector, private sector, regional rural banks (RRBs), and foreign banks.",
        "Key monetary policy instruments include quantitative tools (Repo Rate, Reverse Repo Rate, CRR, SLR) and qualitative credit control tools.",
        "Bank accounts are categorized primarily into Savings, Current, Fixed Deposit (FD), and Recurring Deposit (RD) accounts.",
        "Modern digital banking infrastructure heavily relies on electronic fund transfer systems such as NEFT, RTGS, IMPS, and UPI."
      ],
      "id": "tnxe2he"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3v4x38d",
      "content": "• Banking refers to the business of accepting deposits and providing loans."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pu24foc",
      "content": "• Banks act as financial intermediaries between savers and borrowers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n7ryvwz",
      "content": "• They facilitate economic development by promoting savings and investments."
    },
    {
